Description: Provides a comprehensive, state-aware toolkit for single-cell
    and spatial transcriptomics analysis built around the Bioconductor
    SingleCellExperiment class. It introduces a lightweight analysis-state
    contract to manage dependencies, active context, and provenance across
    workflows. Features include end-to-end preprocessing, dimensionality
    reduction, clustering, multi-backend integration (Harmony, scVI),
    reference mapping (SingleR, Symphony, KNN), trajectory and RNA
    velocity inference (Slingshot, scVelo, RegVelo, CellRank), differential
    expression and enrichment, regulon and gene-set analysis (SCENIC,
    AUCell, GSVA, UCell), cell-cell communication (CellChat, CellPhoneDB,
    NicheNet), rare cell detection, perturbation sensitivity (Augur),
    metacell aggregation (SuperCell), differential abundance (Milo),
    spatial deconvolution (cell2location), spatial colocalization and
    niche detection (SVP), in-silico perturbation (CellOracle), phenotype
    association (scPAS), and enhanced visualization. Python backends are
    isolated via basilisk and exposed as plain R functions.
    Interoperability with AnnData and legacy compatibility aliases are
    supported, but the primary design is centered on
    SingleCellExperiment-native analysis.
